// Activity catalog: every resident is always in exactly one main activity and one of its substates.
// Rates in "effects" are need changes per simulated hour (negative = relief).
// "needs" are utility weights applied to the urgency of each need (0 = satisfied, 1 = desperate).
// "traits" multiply the score: score *= 1 + k * (trait - 0.5) * 2  (k in [-1, 1]).
// "hours": preferred windows [start, end, bonus]; windows may cross midnight.
// Substates with "venue" are selected when the activity happens at that kind of building;
// substates with "auto": true are assigned by the engine from context (groups, transport, events...).
